Well, at last, my first ascension, with a tourist. After trying for
years (a couple of years) with gnomish gealers, I became an expert at
the protection racket. Then I gave other roles a try, and they were
easier (specially kinghts and Tourists). In fact, I haven't played
more than a dozen of Tourists or so. I wasn't specially lucky (I even
had to go through all the temples in the Astral plane), so I must say
that Tourists, against conventional wisdom, are the easiest class. The
protection racket is a breeze with them, and once you get the PYEC,
after a very easy quest, you are unbeatable.

I was granted two wishes before the castle, from a fountain and from a
throne (no magic lamps) - SDSM and Grayswandir. I only used up 5
wishes from the wand, and they were 2 cursed scrolls of genocide, 2
helms of brilliance, a magic marker and another SDSM... I learned the
enchantment limits the hard way.

In the planes, I even meleed the air elementals just for fun, without
going lower than 230 HP. It's really easy to beef up a tourist... more
so if you get 3 magic markers.

